README.md --- Text
 1 # UAC simulation spike
 2 
 3 Rust + TypeScript access lab. The browser uses real WebAuthn APIs with virtual CTAP2 authenticators in the automated tests. Rust verifies genuine signatures. Live Touch ID, phones and hardware security keys remain untested.
 4 
 5 ```sh
 6 cd /Users/master/Documents/Codex/work/uac-spike
 7 just check
 8 just e2e
 9 ```
10 
11 `just check` verifies formatting, TypeScript, Clippy, 24 core tests, license/source/advisory rules, JavaScript advisories and builds. `just e2e` launches isolated headless Chrome and the Rust server, runs 35 browser/API cases, restarts the server to test persisted credentials and revocations, saves screenshots and exits. No user browser profile is used. Ephemeral authenticator keys and test databases are removed at the end.
12 
13 The spike's automated commands obey the deadline in `docs/evidence/budget.json`. For a later explicitly started manual test:
14 
15 ```sh
16 just dev
17 ```
18 
19 Open http://localhost:18240. This separate manual launch is foregrounded and capped at two hours. It is not started automatically. Creating a real passkey requires the operator to confirm the authenticator dialog. Local test data stays under `data/`; `issuer.key` is private and mode 0600. The first registered user owns this artificial lab resource. Production ownership must be provisioned through a separate trusted setup.
20 
21 Browser/device support and HTTPS on a second physical device require the next live test. This local profile is neither UCAN-compatible nor a wallet implementation. Registration/authentication challenges and sessions are transient and become invalid on restart. Credentials, grant revocation and accepted operations persist in SQLite. Revocation is checked again when executing an already-started ceremony.
22 
23 Evidence: `docs/evidence/check.log`, `e2e.json`, `semgrep.json`, per-source Gitleaks reports and three browser screenshots. Audit database freshness and manual-review limits are described in `docs/SPIKE-RESULT.md`.
24 

